     "text": "To add or subtract mixed numbers, first change each one to an improper fraction, then use a common denominator. Example: 2 1/4 + 1/5 = 9/4 + 1/5 = 45/20 + 4/20 = 49/20 = 2 9/20. Write the answer in lowest terms and, if you like, as a mixed number."
    },
